:: StoryTitle
    Live Another Life

:: Start

    <div class='text-center main-title'>\
        <div class='wood-text'>Live Another Life</div>
    </div>
    Welcome to Live Another Life!

    This is a game of choices, developement, advancement, and consequences set in modern day America. But most of all it is freedom. You have the freedom to choose who and what your character is.

    There is nothing physically stopping you from being a poisonious, deceitful, or vindictive person. While you might not be able to make use of your friends to help you accomplish your goals, with enough studying and exploring you will still be able to succeed at whatever it is you seek.

    If you decide to focus soley on your relationships with others, they will be able to help you advance your abilities and offer you assistance quickly, but only up to the extent of their knowledge and experiences.

    There will be no immersion breaking explanations of mechanics or characters. You will learn as you go. Asking questions of your fellow students, reading books, studying tomes, exploring the area, and casting spells will all help you give you more complete understanding of how the world works and what you can do with.

    So go forth and Live Another Life!\
    <div class='text-center'>
        <<button[[New Game | gameWarning]]>><</button>>
    </div>

:: gameWarning

    <span class='red'>CAUTION!</span>
    <em>There can be some dark moments in this game, especially with regards to your backstory. If you are uncomfortable with imagining a severe emotional and physical loss, then I kindly ask you find something else to play. But if you feel like being bold and accepting a difficult rebirth, then I would love for you to continue.</em>
    
    <hr>

    <span class='red'>LAST OTHER WARNING!!!</span>
    <em>There are NSFW elements in this game, both visually and textually. If you are not of legal age to view or read sexually explicit or violent materials in your country, please click the "More Wholesome?" button below to enjoy a more appropriate experience.</em>
    
